=== K1. Lifts of reflection pairs in Spin(7,7) (real Cl(7,7), 128 x 128, exact integers) ===
  (g_a g_b)^2 for a,b both positive (inside E+)   : [-1]
  (g_a g_b)^2 for a,b both negative (inside E-)   : [-1]
  (g_a g_b)^2 for a,b one positive, one negative  : [1]
  => preimage of <r_ab> is Z4 for pp, nn and Z2 x Z2 for pn; restrictions of o: 1, 1, 0
  => o = 1*w2(E+) + 1*w2(E-) + 0*w1^2   (Karoubi: o = w2(E+) + w2(E-))
  => in terms of E = E+ (+) E-: o = w2(E) + w1(E+) w1(E-)   [w2(E) = w2(E+) + w2(E-) + w1(E+) w1(E-)]

=== K2. Stiefel-Whitney classes of C+ and C- (splitting principle, mod 2) ===
  w1(C+) = t;  w1(C-) = t;  w1(l) = t,  w1(X) = s1 + s2 + s3 + t
  w1(C+) = w1(C-) = w1(l): True
  o = w2(C+) + w2(C-) == w2(X) + w1(l)^2 (mod 2): True
  w2(C) = w2(C+) + w2(C-) + w1(C+) w1(C-) == w2(X) (agrees with fiber_signature.out A7): True
  Base (3,1) with c_V c_H < 0, and the overall sign flip (c_V, c_H) -> (-c_V, -c_H), swap or relabel C+ and C-;
  o and w1(C+-) are symmetric under C+ <-> C-, so the result holds in every (7,7) case of Theorem A4.

