=== K4. An RP^2 inside one fiber of Met_(1,3) on which the time line is tautological ===
  g_u = -I + 2 u u^T, u a unit vector in span(e0,e1,e2); g_u = g_{-u}, so u -> g_u factors through RP^2.
  u = (1, 0, 0): eigenvalues {1: 1, -1: 3} (Lorentzian (1,3): True); time line = R u: True
  u = (3/5, 4/5, 0): eigenvalues {-1: 3, 1: 1} (Lorentzian (1,3): True); time line = R u: True
  u = (2/3, 2/3, 1/3): eigenvalues {1: 1, -1: 3} (Lorentzian (1,3): True); time line = R u: True
  u = (0, 5/13, 12/13): eigenvalues {-1: 3, 1: 1} (Lorentzian (1,3): True); time line = R u: True
  So l restricted to this RP^2 is the tautological line gamma, and w1(l)^2 = w1(gamma)^2 != 0 in H^2(RP^2; Z2).
  pi^* w2(X) restricts to 0 on a fiber. Hence o = pi^* w2(X) + w1(l)^2 != 0 on Met(X), for every X.
  On the time-oriented Y' (draft (3.33)) l is oriented, w1(l) = 0, and o = pi^* w2(X).

all checks pass: True
